      "text": "The exponents of the matrix $\\mathbf{A}$ form a cycle of three values: 1, 2, and 3.\nWhen exponent equals 1, the value of the matrix is just $\\begin{pmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}.$\nWhen exponent equals 2, the value is $\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\end{pmatrix}.$\nWhen exponent equals 3, the value is the matrix itself.\nThus, the exponent of $\\mathbf{A}^{100}$ is 100$\\equiv100\\mod3=\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}}$. The answer is 1\\begin{pmatrix}0&0&1\\\\1&0&0\\\\0&1&0\\end{pmatrix}$",
