    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Starting from the definition of matrix multiplication, we can expand $\\mathbf{A}^{100}$ as follows:\n\n\n\n\\[\\mathbf{A}^{100} = \\mathbf{A}^{99} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}.\\]\n\nNext, we can expand $\\mathbf{A}^{99}$ as follows:\n\n\n\n\\[\\mathbf{A}^{99} = \\mathbf{A}^{98} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}.\\]\n\nContinuing this pattern, we eventually get:\n\n\n\n\\[\\mathbf{A}^{99} = \\mathbf{A}^{98} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}.$\n\n\n\nSolving this recurrence relation, we find that $\\mathbf{A}^{100} = \\mathbf{A}^{99} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^2,$ where $\\mathbf{A}^2 = \\mathbf{A}^2.$\n\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n\n\n\\[\\mathbf{A}^{100} = \\mathbf{A}^{99} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^2\\]\n$= \frac{1}{2} \\mathbf{A}^{99} \\cdot 2 \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \\mathbf{A}^{99} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^2.$\n\n\nExpanding cyclically, we get:\n\n\n\n\\[\\mathbf{A}^{99} = \frac{1}{2} \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot 2 \\mathbf{A}^2\\]\n$= \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot \frac{1}{2} 2 \\mathbf{A}^2.$\n\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n\n\n\\[\\mathbf{A}^{100} = \frac{1}{2} \frac{1}{2} \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot 2 \\mathbf{A}^9\\]\n$= (\frac{1}{2} \\mathbf{A}^9) \\cdot (2 \\mathbf{A}^8 \\cdot \\mathbf{A})$\n$= \frac{1}{8} \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot 2 \\mathbf{A}^8 \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \frac{1}{16} \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^8 \\cdot \\mathbf{A}$\n$= \frac{1}{16} \frac{1}{2} \\mathbf{A}^8 \\cdot 2 \\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{A}^7 \\cdot \\mathbf{A}$\n$= \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^8 \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \frac{1}{4} \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot 2 \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^8 \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \frac{1}{8} \\mathbf{A} \\cdot (2 \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^8) \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \frac{1}{16} \\mathbf{A} \\cdot 2 \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^7 \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \frac{1}{32} \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^7 \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^8 \\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{A}^7 \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \frac{1}{16} \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^8 \\cdot (2 \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^8) \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \frac{1}{32} \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^8 \\cdot 2 \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \frac{1}{64} \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^7 \\cdot (2 \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^7) \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^8 \\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{A}^7 \\mathbf{A}^2$\n$= \\mathbf{A}^9 \\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{A}^8 \\mathbf{A}^9$\n$= \\mathbf{A}^{17} \\mathbf{A}^7$\n\n\nBy induction, we conclude that \n\n\\[\\mathbf{A}^n = \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot  \\mathbf{A}^{n-8} = \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^7 \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^5 \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\cdots \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^5\\cdot\\mathbf{A}\\]\n$= \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot  \\mathbf{A}^{18-9} \\mathbf{A}^{17-9} \\mathbf{A}^{16-9} \\mathbf{A}^{15-9} \\mathbf{A}^{14-9} \\mathbf{A}^{13-9} \\mathbf{A}^{12-9} \\mathbf{A}^{11-9} \\mathbf{A}^{10-9} \\mathbf{A}^8 \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^0$\n\nTherefore, \n\n\\[\\mathbf{A}^{100} = \\mathbf{A}^{99} \\cdot \\mathbf{A}^2 = \\left( \\mathbf{A}^9 \\cdot (18 - 9) \\mathbf{A}^{n-9} \\right) \\left(  \\mathbf{A}^{78-9} \\right).\\]\n\nHence, \n\n$\\mathbf{A}^{100} = \frac{1}{2^{50}} \\mathbf{A}^9 \\left( \\mathbf{A}^{5} \\right) \\left( \\mathbf{A}^{5} \\right) \\left( \\mathbf{A}^{5} \\right) \\mathbf{A}^5\\mathbf{A}^5\\left( \frac{1}{2^{50}} \\mathbf{A}^9 \\right)^{20}$\n\n\nand \n\n$\\therefore \\boxed{\\mathbf{A}^{100} = \frac{1}{4^{25}} \\mathbf{A}^{120}  \\mathbf{A}^{240} \\mathbf{A}^{400} \\mathbf{A}^8}.$",
